/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/1/code.py:29:      - If that bottom outer slot already contains a same-color resting
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/1/code.py:30:        diamond, the old rule would still write the complement at the far slot,
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/1/code.py:32:        in the inner slot.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/1/code.py:51:      must check token occupancy before selecting outer vs inner slot.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/1/code.py:53:    - Endpoint rows are moved farther from the token bands so both landing slots
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/1/code.py:58:      slot, so the solver can unambiguously interpret every input token as a
